// Dogwood port of policies/escalate.cedar. escalate requires a non-empty reason.
// Dogwood has no trim(); this catches the empty string, which is what the Nova Sonic
// tool call will actually send if the model omits a reason (the field is required in
// schema.json, but Policy is the independent check). Whitespace-only reasons ("   ")
// pass this and are caught by outbound_ivr.tools.business.escalate in the Lambda, same as
// record_item's per-case check.
//
// Deliberately NOT ported here: the LiveKit-mode-only rule in
// src/outbound_ivr/voice/agent.py ("First bring in a colleague with transfer_to_team") that
// refuses escalate until transfer_to_team has been tried and failed on this call,
// unless there is no team_dialer to try it with at all. A Dogwood temporal rule can
// express "transfer_to_team was attempted this session" (`formerly within` against
// AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___transfer_to_team"::request, see
// policies/dogwood/transfer_to_team.dw for the same action name) -- see "Require a
// prerequisite action", https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/
// example-policies-temporal.html#example-policies-temporal-sequencing. It cannot
// express "...unless there is no team_dialer for this session", because whether a
// team_dialer exists is an application-level fact (which transport/backend this call
// is running on) that never reaches the Gateway as an event; Dogwood's only documented
// information provider beyond its event history is Amazon Bedrock Guardrails
// (policy-temporal.html), nothing that exposes app configuration. Both Asterisk mode
// and LiveKit mode call escalate through the one Gateway/Policy engine this repo
// deploys (infra/stacks/agentcore_stack.py); Asterisk mode never calls
// transfer_to_team at all (docs/escalation-handoff.md: "Asterisk mode keeps escalate
// exactly as it is today... nothing in this file changes that path"). A temporal rule
// requiring a prior transfer_to_team attempt would therefore deny every Asterisk-mode
// escalate unconditionally, which contradicts that doc. The ordering rule stays
// enforced only in src/outbound_ivr/voice/agent.py, which does have the team_dialer/mode
// context to apply it correctly; see policies/README.md for the full writeup.
permit(
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___escalate",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${GATEWAY_ARN}"
) when {
  context.input has reason &&
  context.input.reason != "" &&
  context.input has case_id &&
  context.input.case_id != ""
};
